* <translate><!--T:76--> "BIOU" logo ([<tvar name=1>http://web.archive.org/web/20210714101951/http://5b0988e595225.cdn.sohucs.com/images/20180821/a267e6686dfc41cbb079f0799a1feaa4.jpeg</tvar> image]), with letter "b" and "o", and a small barcode in the upper right corner, is not copyrightable for lacking originality, ruled Higher People's Court of Beijing Municipality in 2018 ([<tvar name=2>http://web.archive.org/web/20210714102139/https://www.bjcourt.gov.cn/cpws/paperView.htm?id=100944797703</tvar> final judgement] and related articles [<tvar name=3>http://web.archive.org/web/20210714102129/https://www.sohu.com/a/249071694_448643</tvar>] [<tvar name=4>https://web.archive.org/web/20210714102329/https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/jdVNJ50HmfqoZfWMFTT57A</tvar>]). Note that the logo was initially ruled as copyrightable by the Trademark Review and Adjudication Board and a lower court.</translate>
* <translate><!--T:77--> "KON" logo (see below), with three black bars crossed together, is not copyrightable for lacking originality, ruled Beijing Dongcheng District People's Court in 2019 ([<tvar name=1>https://web.archive.org/web/20210714185402/https://www.bjcourt.gov.cn/cpws/paperView.htm?id=100878981336</tvar> final judgement] and [<tvar name=3>https://www.macrumors.com/2017/12/19/apple-app-store-logo-trademark-lawsuit/</tvar> news coverage]).</translate>
